gather current share structure for reverse split calculation.

.why = we need to know current issued and authorized shares to calculate the split ratio.

---

## required fields

| field | your info | source |
|-------|-----------|--------|
| corporation name | | Delaware search |
| file number | | Delaware search |
| authorized shares | | Delaware search or Certificate of Incorporation |
| issued shares | | stock ledger, Founder Stock Board Consent |
| par value | | Certificate of Incorporation |
| shareholders | | stock ledger |

---

## target structure

to qualify for the **$175/year tax floor** (Authorized Shares Method):
- authorized shares must be ≤ 5,000
- issued shares must be ≤ authorized

| field | current | target |
|-------|---------|--------|
| authorized | | ≤ 5,000 |
| issued | | ≤ 5,000 |

### ⚠️ $175 is the TAX. the annual bill is $225.

> 🚩 **this line used to read "to qualify for $175/year." corrected
> 2026-09-02** — it named the goal of this entire route and dropped the word
> that scopes it.

| item | amount |
|------|-------:|
| franchise tax at ≤5,000 authorized | **$175.00** |
| annual report fee, non-exempt domestic corporation | **$50.00** |
| **annual floor** | **$225.00** |

the tax figure is `franchise.tax.delaware --authorized 5000 …`, which prints
`⬅️ tax only` beside it. the $50 is quoted from the Division of Corporations at
`corp.delaware.gov/frtax/` (an **exempt** domestic corporation pays $25).

⚠️ the report fee is owed **before and after** the reduction, so it cancels out
of any *savings* figure — which is why step 6 of the reinstate route correctly
states the delta as `$400 − $175`. it does **not** cancel out of your bill, and
this stone states a **level**, not a delta.

